1
00:00:21,480 --> 00:00:22,440
Who taught you to wear makeup?

2
00:00:24,199 --> 00:00:25,120
Do you have any idea

3
00:00:25,199 --> 00:00:27,039
how bad this makeup is for your skin?

4
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:33,359
Everyone else is Preparing for the Gaokao.

5
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:35,159
Pucker up.

6
00:00:36,399 --> 00:00:37,920
Going to school wearing makeup like this,

7
00:00:38,600 --> 00:00:40,159
what would your teachers and classmates think?

8
00:00:40,960 --> 00:00:41,640
Pucker them up.

9
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:49,479
Your lips.

10
00:00:50,399 --> 00:00:51,000
Close your eyes.

11
00:00:52,640 --> 00:00:53,719
You need to focus

12
00:00:53,719 --> 00:00:55,880
on what matters—your studies.

13
00:00:56,880 --> 00:00:57,479
Do you hear me?

14
00:01:00,359 --> 00:01:00,960
It hurts.

15
00:01:01,960 --> 00:01:02,560
Bear with it.

16
00:01:05,719 --> 00:01:06,280
All done.

17
00:01:07,280 --> 00:01:07,959
Take a look now.

18
00:01:10,920 --> 00:01:11,599
So much prettier.

19
00:01:14,239 --> 00:01:15,359
Mom's just doing this for your own good.

20
00:01:27,719 --> 00:01:30,280
That's it for our date today.

21
00:01:35,799 --> 00:01:38,719
About the question you just asked me...

22
00:01:40,040 --> 00:01:41,200
Don't rush to answer.

23
00:01:42,040 --> 00:01:43,120
Give yourself a little more time.

24
00:01:47,040 --> 00:01:47,799
I'll give you my answer tomorrow.

25
00:01:48,920 --> 00:01:50,359
Okay, I'll wait for you.

26
00:01:53,439 --> 00:01:54,120
Wait a minute.

27
00:01:56,799 --> 00:01:57,400
Here.

28
00:02:19,400 --> 00:02:20,400
I think

29
00:02:21,439 --> 00:02:22,840
it's not as serious as you say.

30
00:02:23,520 --> 00:02:26,000
It just means giving her more time.

31
00:02:26,680 --> 00:02:28,280
We each just need to spare a bit.

32
00:02:30,080 --> 00:02:31,479
It's not as easy as you say.

33
00:02:31,759 --> 00:02:32,520
Have you ever thought about it?

34
00:02:33,039 --> 00:02:34,439
They're not just dating.

35
00:02:34,439 --> 00:02:35,759
They'll start a family in the future.

36
00:02:35,960 --> 00:02:36,879
They'll even have kids.

37
00:02:37,080 --> 00:02:39,159
And later on, the kids will go to school.

38
00:02:39,319 --> 00:02:40,840
And they'll have to help them find jobs.

39
00:02:41,840 --> 00:02:42,960
You're getting way ahead of yourself.

40
00:02:43,080 --> 00:02:44,680
You're just being short-sighted.

41
00:02:52,159 --> 00:02:53,400
Actually, I think

42
00:02:53,599 --> 00:02:55,360
if we each squeeze out an hour or two,

43
00:02:55,759 --> 00:02:56,599
it's totally doable.

44
00:02:57,159 --> 00:02:58,199
That's enough for my workouts anyway.

45
00:02:59,599 --> 00:03:00,439
Sure, it's enough for you,

46
00:03:00,680 --> 00:03:01,879
but what about her makeup job?

47
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:02,879
Is she going to keep doing it?

48
00:03:03,319 --> 00:03:04,560
Stop using others as an excuse.

49
00:03:05,159 --> 00:03:05,840
I think

50
00:03:05,840 --> 00:03:07,520
you're just worried about your game time.

51
00:03:07,960 --> 00:03:08,840
Those crappy games of yours,

52
00:03:09,159 --> 00:03:10,400
playing them or not makes no difference.

53
00:03:11,439 --> 00:03:12,680
Oh, and your workouts are useful?

54
00:03:12,879 --> 00:03:15,360
Will those muscles put food on the table?

55
00:03:15,680 --> 00:03:16,840
They can't put food on the table,

56
00:03:17,199 --> 00:03:19,719
but they're enough to crush your skull!

57
00:04:06,719 --> 00:04:07,560
Maybe

58
00:04:10,719 --> 00:04:12,360
us disappearing together

59
00:04:13,560 --> 00:04:14,719
is the best choice.

60
00:04:17,959 --> 00:04:21,040
You don't have to say that out of anger.

61
00:04:21,800 --> 00:04:22,639
I'm serious.

62
00:04:28,279 --> 00:04:29,160
Just like you said,

63
00:04:30,759 --> 00:04:32,560
she'll get caught up in life's trifles,

64
00:04:34,279 --> 00:04:35,199
but who knows,

65
00:04:36,279 --> 00:04:37,279
that might be exactly what she wants.

66
00:04:39,720 --> 00:04:41,120
The reason we exist

67
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:43,360
is because of past regrets.

68
00:04:45,040 --> 00:04:51,199
If she loses Liang Chuan because of us,

69
00:04:53,160 --> 00:04:54,399
wouldn't we repeat the same mistake?

70
00:04:59,199 --> 00:04:59,680
It's not that I

71
00:04:59,680 --> 00:05:01,279
refuse to give up my time.

72
00:05:01,879 --> 00:05:03,319
But whether she really likes Liang Chuan,

73
00:05:04,120 --> 00:05:05,160
we have no idea.

74
00:05:06,360 --> 00:05:06,879
Yeah.

75
00:05:08,720 --> 00:05:11,759
She has to decide this for herself.

76
00:05:25,680 --> 00:05:28,040
Teacher Lin! Teacher Lin!

77
00:05:29,959 --> 00:05:31,360
Are we drawing you again today?

78
00:05:34,360 --> 00:05:35,079
Today,

79
00:05:37,920 --> 00:05:38,959
you're drawing yourselves.

80
00:06:52,680 --> 00:06:53,480
Let's talk.

81
00:06:54,160 --> 00:06:56,120
The male lead is here.

82
00:06:57,560 --> 00:06:58,199
Okay.

83
00:07:03,720 --> 00:07:04,680
I've thought about it.

84
00:07:05,360 --> 00:07:06,199
Thought about what?

85
00:07:06,600 --> 00:07:07,560
You asked me yesterday,

86
00:07:08,199 --> 00:07:09,040
out of the four Lin Ran personas,

87
00:07:09,720 --> 00:07:10,959
which one I like best.

88
00:07:11,839 --> 00:07:12,480
Right.

89
00:07:13,199 --> 00:07:15,000
But I think that question

90
00:07:15,279 --> 00:07:17,040
is fundamentally flawed.

91
00:07:18,600 --> 00:07:19,279
Why?

92
00:07:21,079 --> 00:07:21,759
To be honest,

93
00:07:21,959 --> 00:07:23,240
sometimes I really wonder

94
00:07:23,519 --> 00:07:24,800
if, at a certain moment,

95
00:07:24,800 --> 00:07:26,560
you were actually possessed by someone.

96
00:07:32,079 --> 00:07:33,920
But I quickly dismissed that idea.

97
00:07:35,240 --> 00:07:37,360
Do you know why?

98
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:43,439
Because I've always believed

99
00:07:47,240 --> 00:07:48,319
that you are just you.

100
00:07:53,079 --> 00:07:54,439
Even though at different times,

101
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:57,439
your temper and habits might differ,

102
00:07:59,439 --> 00:08:00,360
but

103
00:08:02,720 --> 00:08:03,600
your earnestness,

104
00:08:07,040 --> 00:08:07,720
persistence,

105
00:08:09,879 --> 00:08:10,879
and gentleness

106
00:08:13,759 --> 00:08:15,000
have never changed.

107
00:08:19,959 --> 00:08:22,639
When did you figure that out?

108
00:08:26,920 --> 00:08:28,240
From your gaze.

109
00:08:30,759 --> 00:08:32,000
When I look into your eyes,

110
00:08:33,399 --> 00:08:34,519
I can feel it.

111
00:08:36,799 --> 00:08:37,759
My gaze?

112
00:08:39,159 --> 00:08:40,120
What kind of gaze did you give him?

113
00:08:42,559 --> 00:08:43,480
The same as yours.

114
00:08:49,440 --> 00:08:50,320
So,

115
00:08:51,240 --> 00:08:53,840
you doubt there are four Lin Ran personas.

116
00:08:57,440 --> 00:08:58,360
But you're special.

117
00:08:59,080 --> 00:09:01,879
Like four Lin Ran from other timelines

118
00:09:02,240 --> 00:09:03,519
sharing the same body.

119
00:09:15,879 --> 00:09:16,919
Then let me ask a different question.

120
00:09:17,679 --> 00:09:19,000
Even if there are four Lin Ran personas,

121
00:09:19,440 --> 00:09:22,360
there must be one you prefer to be with.

122
00:09:32,320 --> 00:09:33,200
What are you hoping for?

123
00:09:34,759 --> 00:09:35,399
Nothing.

124
00:09:37,240 --> 00:09:39,120
If I had to choose,

125
00:09:41,360 --> 00:09:42,759
I think I'd choose the original Lin Ran.

126
00:09:50,600 --> 00:09:51,720
Let's go, let's go.

127
00:10:00,039 --> 00:10:00,759
Where were you?

128
00:10:01,799 --> 00:10:02,679
We missed you.

129
00:10:03,360 --> 00:10:05,200
Move, move. Make way.

130
00:10:07,559 --> 00:10:09,759
I just don't know how to face you all.

131
00:10:09,960 --> 00:10:12,000
You don't need to know how to face us.

132
00:10:12,919 --> 00:10:15,519
Now, you only need to face one person.

133
00:10:17,440 --> 00:10:19,000
He already gave you his answer.

134
00:10:19,360 --> 00:10:20,120
Go on.

135
00:10:21,960 --> 00:10:23,440
I haven't figured it out yet.

136
00:10:23,759 --> 00:10:24,559
Cut the nonsense.

137
00:10:24,559 --> 00:10:25,559
Let's go. Move, move, move.

138
00:10:31,360 --> 00:10:33,120
Where did you go?

139
00:10:34,559 --> 00:10:35,279
I...

140
00:10:36,080 --> 00:10:37,399
I just saw the principal walking by,

141
00:10:37,399 --> 00:10:38,360
so I said hello.

142
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:45,559
The question you asked me earlier...

143
00:10:46,039 --> 00:10:47,039
I already answered it.

144
00:10:48,559 --> 00:10:49,879
Can I ask you a question?

145
00:10:54,279 --> 00:10:57,919
Would you like to officially date me?

146
00:11:04,480 --> 00:11:05,080
I...

147
00:11:12,840 --> 00:11:13,519
I'm sorry.

148
00:11:14,799 --> 00:11:15,399
I can't.

149
00:11:19,120 --> 00:11:19,759
Why?

150
00:11:21,159 --> 00:11:22,840
Because I'm not ready yet

151
00:11:22,840 --> 00:11:24,320
to take on the responsibilities,

152
00:11:25,519 --> 00:11:27,799
nor am I ready to lose what I have.

153
00:11:29,519 --> 00:11:30,320
I have a condition.

154
00:11:30,600 --> 00:11:31,679
Don't talk. Don't talk.

155
00:11:32,320 --> 00:11:33,240
What condition?

156
00:11:34,080 --> 00:11:36,559
Two people together need to compromise.

157
00:11:36,559 --> 00:11:37,720
I agree with that.

158
00:11:38,159 --> 00:11:40,039
But I don't want to lose myself.

159
00:11:40,559 --> 00:11:41,519
Most of the time,

160
00:11:41,679 --> 00:11:43,639
I'll be the Teacher Lin you know well.

161
00:11:43,919 --> 00:11:46,159
But at certain moments,

162
00:11:46,240 --> 00:11:48,159
if I really want to play games,

163
00:11:48,159 --> 00:11:49,360
if I want to work out,

164
00:11:49,360 --> 00:11:51,159
or if I want to continue my makeup career,

165
00:11:51,360 --> 00:11:53,600
you have to support me.

166
00:11:53,879 --> 00:11:54,799
And respect me.

167
00:11:55,080 --> 00:11:55,919
Can you do that?

168
00:12:01,600 --> 00:12:05,639
Is that your only condition?

169
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:06,840
Yes, that's it.

170
00:12:09,320 --> 00:12:10,000
I agree.

171
00:12:12,080 --> 00:12:13,559
I like you exactly the way you are now.

172
00:12:14,559 --> 00:12:16,000
You don't need to change a thing.

173
00:12:19,399 --> 00:12:20,200
Lin Ran.

174
00:12:22,080 --> 00:12:23,799
I like how in everything you do,

175
00:12:24,919 --> 00:12:26,120
you always try your hardest.

176
00:12:44,279 --> 00:12:45,039
So...

177
00:12:46,279 --> 00:12:48,200
I guess we're officially dating.

178
00:13:00,399 --> 00:13:01,120
Alright.

179
00:13:21,960 --> 00:13:22,840
Did you ask?

180
00:13:23,279 --> 00:13:24,480
He's really not going to the internet cafe?

181
00:13:25,279 --> 00:13:27,600
I told you, we made plans to go hiking.

182
00:13:27,720 --> 00:13:28,320
Hiking?

183
00:13:28,720 --> 00:13:29,679
I'm good at that!

184
00:13:29,879 --> 00:13:31,120
I'll definitely Crush him!

185
00:13:31,200 --> 00:13:32,720
Bro, they're going on a date.

186
00:13:32,720 --> 00:13:33,759
It's not a boot camp.

187
00:13:34,279 --> 00:13:36,039
All you think about is working out.

188
00:13:36,159 --> 00:13:36,679
All right, all right.

189
00:13:36,679 --> 00:13:37,879
Give it a rest, both of you.

190
00:13:37,879 --> 00:13:39,360
We agreed today it's just the two of us.

191
00:13:39,360 --> 00:13:40,159
Just the two of us are going.

192
00:13:40,919 --> 00:13:43,039
Wait, are you Ditching friends for love?

193
00:13:43,519 --> 00:13:45,759
Plus, you're a bit ungrateful too.

194
00:13:45,759 --> 00:13:46,840
What are you even talking about?

195
00:13:47,039 --> 00:13:47,919
Don't you forget.

196
00:13:48,080 --> 00:13:50,879
We're also among the people he likes.

197
00:13:52,120 --> 00:13:52,840
Just speak for yourself.

198
00:13:52,840 --> 00:13:53,799
Don't drag me into this.

199
00:14:00,120 --> 00:14:00,879
All right.

200
00:14:01,759 --> 00:14:02,279
All right.

201
00:14:04,039 --> 00:14:04,840
Does this look good?

202
00:14:13,440 --> 00:14:14,159
It looks good.

203
00:14:14,879 --> 00:14:16,600
I'm going to get changed then.

204
00:14:21,639 --> 00:14:22,720
So beautiful.

205
00:14:24,159 --> 00:14:27,279
Do you guys think they'll kiss today?

206
00:15:05,279 --> 00:15:06,679
What should we do next?

207
00:15:12,279 --> 00:15:12,759
Let's walk over there.

208
00:15:12,759 --> 00:15:13,480
Sure.

209
00:16:12,159 --> 00:16:12,960
Do you want to kiss?

210
00:16:13,519 --> 00:16:14,159
Come over here.

211
00:16:14,639 --> 00:16:15,440
Alright.

212
00:16:37,200 --> 00:16:39,000
I think I lost my bag.
